Phase 2 — Install Docker on EC2
Run each command one by one in your EC2 terminal:

Step 1 — Update server packages
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

Step 2 — Install Docker
sudo apt install docker.io -y

Step 3 — Start and enable Docker
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker

Step 4 — Allow running Docker without sudo
sudo usermod -aG docker ubuntu
newgrp docker

Step 5 — Install Docker Compose
sudo apt install docker-compose -y

Step 6 — Verify installation
docker --version
docker-compose --version
Tip: You should see version numbers printed. If so, Docker is ready!


